+    // 26.8 GiB engram, then ~18k faults across 127 generated tokens. Paid for in
+    // full; used a rounding error at a time.
+    //
+    // `no_host` is the right condition: it already means "CPU-placed weights
+    // must be genuinely pageable", the local-fit gate discounts those bytes on
+    // exactly that promise, and MAP_POPULATE breaks it. Weights that ARE
+    // streamed into device buffers keep their readahead — the fd still carries
+    // POSIX_FADV_SEQUENTIAL and llama_mmap's whole-file MADV_RANDOM is gated on
+    // `numa`, not on prefetch.
+    ml.init_mappings(!params.no_host, use_mlock ? &pimpl->mlock_mmaps : nullptr);
